# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DeepSeek Harness — web profile Cordis patch template.
# Rendered to ~/.config/agent/dsh/cordis.patch.yml and symlinked to
# ~/.dsh/profiles/web/cordis.patch.yml (dsh reads the patch fresh on
# every request; no restart needed for config edits).
#
# RESEARCH FINDINGS (pinned 2026-10-24; developer preview — re-verify
# on upstream breaking changes):
#
# 1. Config location + format. DSH keeps per-profile user patches as
#    YAML at $DSH_HOME/profiles/<profile>/cordis.patch.yml (a list of
#    Cordis patch entries, one per plugin row), plus a machine-local
#    home-level $DSH_HOME/cordis.patch.yml that outranks it.
#    $DSH_HOME defaults to ~/.dsh. For the standard `dsh web` launch
#    the profile is `web`, so the file this template renders to is
#    ~/.dsh/profiles/web/cordis.patch.yml.
#    Sources: https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/blob/master/apps/cli/README.md
#    and apps/cli/reference/README.md (patch composition / DSH_HOME default).
#
# 2. Env-var indirection: SUPPORTED. A provider's `apiKeyEnv` is a
#    credential reference resolved per request through the harness
#    credential seam — "no secret enters the configuration file"
#    (packages/llm/llm-pi-ai/README.md). So the template renders the
#    VARIABLE NAME into apiKeyEnv and the API key value never
#    touches this file: dsh reads it from the process environment at
#    runtime (interactive shells get it via secrets.env sourcing).
#
# 3. Provider shape (pi-ai custom route): a route the installed catalog
#    does not ship needs `api` (wire protocol: openai-completions,
#    openai-responses, or anthropic-messages), `baseURL`, and a
#    non-empty `models` list. `apiKeyEnv` names the env var holding the
#    key. Sources: packages/llm/llm-pi-ai/README.md,
#    docs/user/guide/providers.md (custom model API).
#
# 4. Renderer. The file is YAML, so render_json does not apply: dsh/
#    install.sh ships its own python3 renderer (UPPER_SNAKE placeholders
#    become json.dumps(value), which is a valid YAML 1.2 double-quoted
#    scalar, so URLs/model ids/paths are safe without PyYAML),
#    structurally validated with PyYAML when it is importable. Values
#    reach the render process through the environment only — never argv.
#
# 5. Defaults. Base URL and model id fall back to DeepSeek's OFFICIAL
#    public endpoint/model (public information); a private gateway or a
#    private model id is a secret — set DSH_LLM_BASE_URL /
#    DSH_LLM_MODEL (or the shared LLM_* layer) and re-run the installer.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
- id: llm-pi-ai
  config:
    providers:
      shared-llm:
        apiKeyEnv: $__DSH_API_KEY_ENV__
        api: openai-completions
        baseURL: $__DSH_LLM_BASE_URL__
        models:
          - id: $__DSH_LLM_MODEL__
